Done @soyuka — `MappingAwareTransformCallableInterface` now **extends `TransformCallableInterface`** and receives the `Map` as a fourth `__invoke()` argument, so the `withMapping()` wither is gone and a transformer implements a single interface and stays stateless.

```php
interface MappingAwareTransformCallableInterface extends TransformCallableInterface
{
    public function __invoke(mixed $value, object $source, ?object $target, ?Map $map = null): mixed;
}
```

The fourth parameter is optional (`?Map $map = null`) so the child signature stays LSP-compatible with the parent (PHP rejects an extra *required* parameter when extending an interface); `ObjectMapper::applyTransforms()` always forwards the real mapping.

